<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim Dabo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1846</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim Dabo was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> from 1819 to 1846, the second ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> created by the Fulani jihad within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>. He suppressed revolts, strengthened the emirate's administration and promoted trade and learning. His descendants, the Dabo dynasty, have provided Kano's emirs ever since.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibrahim-dabo.jpg" alt="Ibrahim Dabo" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bohr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Unconfirmed_Kano_Flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
